#
# Correctness scaffold for the client-Boost hypothesis in ModHE/MLWE-CKKS:
#   1. client encrypts at low rank r_c and only one base modulus q_0;
#   2. server performs a proper key-switching rank-up r_c -> r_E;
#   3. server performs a toy ModRaise/q0->Q scaffold that materializes all RNS
#      shares from the q0 ciphertext, so the object has the expected full-chain
